{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connected component is solved alone; a vertex adjacent to all the others of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component answers alone. Otherwise branch and reduce: after every choice, an undominated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with one possible dominator gets it, and a vertex whose undominated closed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neighbourhood lies in another’s is ruled out (for the lexicographic pass only in favour of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a lesser vertex, which keeps the least set; this leaf rule settles paths and many trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outright). The search branches on the most-coverage dominator of an undominated vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the fewest left and prunes on the budget, on the largest coverages, and on a greedy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2-packing (vertices with no dominator in common, each needing its own; on trees the largest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2-packing is γ, Meir and Moon 1975). γ comes from a greedy descent and decisions one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smaller; the least set of γ vertices is then decided vertex by vertex in index order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"against a witness, each decision searching only the part of the problem the vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"touches. Sparse components keep O(n + m) words of state; dense ones (mean degree d with d²"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"above c ⌈c \/ 64⌉) use bitset closed neighbourhoods, under 2m words. Exponential in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component size in the worst case."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","title":"minimumDominatingSet()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumDominatingSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE20minimumDominatingSetSay6VertexQzGyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1846","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum dominating set (exact): every vertex is in it or adjacent to one in it, and of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the smallest such sets it is the lexicographically least by vertex index (the rule of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Self-loops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parallel edges do not matter; isolated vertices are in it.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumdominatingset()"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/covering","title":"Covering","type":"topic","abstract":[]},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumDominatingSet()":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumDominatingSet()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex",